"""
Loads a WHO-aligned standard catalogue.

    python manage.py seed_catalogue

**Provenance, stated plainly.** These 600+ entries are transcribed from the
Ethiopian Essential Medicines List, 7th edition (EFDA/GDL/067, October 2024,
EFDA/Ministry of Health) — itself explicitly harmonised with the WHO Model
List of Essential Medicines, 23rd edition (2023). Every generic name,
dosage form and strength traces to that document. They are marked
`data_source = WHO_EML` accordingly. `atc_code` is filled in only where the
transcriber was confident of it and left blank otherwise, and
`efda_registration_number` is always left blank rather than invented,
because a wrong registration number on a regulatory return is worse than a
missing one.

This is the *essential* medicines list — the deliberately curated subset a
health system is built around, not a registry of every product licensed for
sale. If a pharmacy needs the complete EFDA-registered product list (every
brand, every pack, essential or not), that has to come from EFDA's own
register (see docs/CATALOGUE_IMPORT.md) via `import_catalogue`, which
overwrites these rows in place (matching is on generic name + strength +
form + brand) rather than duplicating them.
"""
